gth: 1,250 m" [:br {}] "Height Differential: 23 m" [:br {}] "Maximum Climb: 21 m" [:br {}] "Total Climbing: 31 m"]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "There were no surprises in the semi-final round; all the top nations qualified comfortably for the final. In the final, Norway was second to Finland at the first exchange. But the final was essentially decided when a spurt from " [:a {:href "/athletes/101008"} "Marit Bjørgen"] " established a lead of about three seconds over Finland and Sweden during the second leg. Although her teammate " [:a {:href "/athletes/128189"} "Ingvild Flugstad Østberg"] " allowed the gap to close a little on the third leg, Bjørgen extended the lead again on the fourth leg and the final result was never really in doubt. Finland, represented by " [:a {:href "/athletes/110053"} "Aino-Kaisa Saarinen"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/127662"} "Kerttu Niskanen"] ", were comfortable silver-medal winners, about nine seconds behind Norway."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Sweden’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/118767"} "Ida Ingemarsdotter"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/128586"} "Stina Nilsson"] " took the bronze medals, leading Germany’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/109789"} "Stefanie Böhler"] " and " [:a {:href "/athletes/127819"} "Denise Herrmann"] " by little more than a second, when Nilsson overtook Herrmann on the final few meters. " [:a {:href "/athletes/109782"} "Justyna Kowalczyk"] " led Poland to fifth place, leaving only sixth place for the Russian home team."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Number"] [:th {} "Pair"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {:class "bib"} "–"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/128189"} "Ingvild Flugstad Østberg"] " / " [:a {:href "/athletes/101008"} "Marit Bjørgen"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/NOR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.co